  "description": "timing.v1 §2.5: one reader's deadline tracker for one provider and resource -> the reports it makes. deadline_ms is the resource's deadline; bound is the resource's bound (core §2.7), null for none; known lists the members the reader can name without hearing them. events are in order, each at_ms an instant of the reader's monotonic clock in milliseconds, exact to the nanosecond: start (the subscription declared), arrival of member (expired true: an expired sample, which is no arrival, §2.6), owner with state present, unconfirmed or absent (the owner's token as the reader observes it, v1.md §0), member_gone (a complete read shows no member token of member), and tick (an instant the reader judges at). At every event's instant the reader first judges every member it holds, in member order (byte order of the names): a member heard is missed when the instant is more than deadline_ms after its last arrival (due = last arrival + deadline), a known member never heard and waited for when it is more than deadline_ms after the instant its wait began (due = that instant + deadline); then a member that is not known, missed, and whose last arrival is 3,600,000 ms or more before the instant is forgotten. Then it applies the event. start: each known member is waited for from the later of the start and the instant the owner became present, if the owner is present. arrival (ignored before start, and when expired): a held member becomes heard at that instant, reporting met if it was missed; a member not held is held, heard, when fewer than bound members are held, else reported beyond_bound and not held; a first arrival reports nothing. owner present: from unseen or absent, the owner became present at that instant, and every known member never heard and not ended is waited for from it (if started); from unconfirmed, nothing changes. owner unconfirmed: nothing changes but the state. owner absent: every waited-for member is no longer waited for (a missed one stays missed). member_gone: a held member ends, reported ended (reason gone) when it was heard or missed; a known member stays held, not waited for, until its next arrival; another is no longer held. A forgotten member is reported ended (reason forgotten) and no longer held. Known members are always held, count toward the bound, and are never forgotten. expect.transitions are the reports in order: missed (member, due_ms, by_ms = due + max(deadline/50, 1 ms), and owner, the owner's state at the report: present, unconfirmed, absent, or unseen when no state was given), met, ended (reason), beyond_bound; each at_ms the instant it is reported. expect.held is the members held after the last event, in member order; expect.next_due_ms the earliest due among held members heard or waited for, null when none."
}
